From b87276ec9d5c86234077dfbdcbeae9aeab41e4fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:51:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] ap: Default the DHCP router to the AP address

iwd.ap(5) documents that [IPv4].Gateway falls back to the local IP
address, but nothing implements the fallback since ell's DHCP server
stopped defaulting the gateway to its own address (ell commit 77cef25,
"dhcp-server: Omit OPTION_ROUTER if not configured").  An AP started
without a Gateway setting, which includes every AP started through
the AccessPoint.Start() D-Bus method, hands out leases with no Router
option, so clients get an address but no default route and cannot
reach anything beyond the AP's subnet.

Use the AP's own address when no gateway is configured, for both the
DHCP server and the FILS IP Address Assignment response.
---
 src/ap.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap.c b/src/ap.c
index 416e1104..39e8d0f5 100644
--- a/src/ap.c
+++ b/src/ap.c
@@ -3299,7 +3299,16 @@ static int ap_setup_netconfig4(struct ap_state *ap, const char **addr_str_list,
 		goto cleanup;
 	}
 
-	if (gateway_str && !l_dhcp_server_set_gateway(dhcp, gateway_str)) {
+	/*
+	 * Without a configured gateway, advertise the AP itself as the
+	 * router as iwd.ap(5) documents.  The DHCP server omits the Router
+	 * option entirely when no gateway is set, leaving clients without a
+	 * default route.
+	 */
+	if (!gateway_str)
+		gateway_str = addr_str_buf;
+
+	if (!l_dhcp_server_set_gateway(dhcp, gateway_str)) {
 		l_error("l_dhcp_server_set_gateway failed");
 		goto cleanup;
 	}
